We love to
cook together.

13:45.068 --> 13:46.567
Uh, correction,
I love to cook,

13:46.569 --> 13:48.169
he loves to eat.

13:48.171 --> 13:51.272
See? This is what
I wanted to see.

13:51.274 --> 13:53.041
The two of you just
being yourselves.

13:53.043 --> 13:54.008
Happy, relaxed.

13:54.010 --> 13:55.943
Oh, I'll get that.

13:55.945 --> 13:57.945
If you really want
to see us relaxed

13:57.947 --> 13:59.681
you should come by
for brunch someday.

13:59.683 --> 14:02.383
The Mary's are bloody
and the Lorraine's are quiche.

14:02.385 --> 14:05.119
Oh, I can see why
you fell in love with him.

14:05.121 --> 14:07.488
Really?

14:07.490 --> 14:10.224
What did you see exactly?

14:11.561 --> 14:13.695
Alan!

14:13.697 --> 14:15.630
Lyndsey?

14:15.632 --> 14:16.931
Um, have you
been drinking?

14:16.933 --> 14:20.501
Uh, ding-ding-ding,
we have a wiener...

14:20.503 --> 14:21.903
Whoa, whoa,
okay, okay, shh!

14:21.905 --> 14:23.137
W-What are you
doing here?

14:23.139 --> 14:25.673
Well, you said
you and Walden

14:25.675 --> 14:27.542
are just getting married
to get a kid.

14:27.544 --> 14:30.878
So, there's no reason you can't
have sex with me on the side.

14:30.880 --> 14:32.680
You know, the “DL.”

14:32.682 --> 14:35.550
That means “Do Lyndsey.”

14:35.552 --> 14:38.453
Okay, okay, okay, this
is not a good time.

14:38.455 --> 14:39.954
Uh, the-the social
worker's here.

14:39.956 --> 14:41.189
Oh, that's great!

14:41.191 --> 14:42.790
I can help you guys.

14:42.792 --> 14:45.093
I can tell her that
you'll be good parents.

14:45.095 --> 14:47.261
And I know because
I'm a g... Oh.

14:48.765 --> 14:50.832
...mother.

14:50.834 --> 14:52.934
Okay, um...

14:52.936 --> 14:55.470
maybe-maybe we should go
to my room a-and talk.

14:55.472 --> 14:59.474
I won't be able to talk much,
'cause my mouth will be full.

14:59.476 --> 15:00.541
Wink, wink.

15:00.543 --> 15:03.411
Hopefully with breath mints.

15:04.547 --> 15:07.648
You wait in here and I will
call a cab to take you home.

15:07.650 --> 15:11.452
My home is in your pants.

15:11.454 --> 15:13.988
What happened? Why did
you start drinking again?

15:13.990 --> 15:15.857
Well, 'cause you married Walden.

15:15.859 --> 15:18.459
The only person in your life
who's prettier than me.

15:18.461 --> 15:20.695
But you know we're just
doing that to get a kid.

15:20.697 --> 15:23.364
Yeah, but if I wasn't
so screwed up last year,

15:23.366 --> 15:24.932
then we would still be together.

15:24.934 --> 15:27.201
Then we could get married
and have a baby.

15:27.203 --> 15:29.070
We could sell that baby
to Walden.

15:29.072 --> 15:31.005
'Cause let's face it,

15:31.007 --> 15:32.940
we don't want to raise
another kid,

15:32.942 --> 15:34.776
'cause both our kids suck.

15:34.778 --> 15:37.412
Okay, uh, refreshing,
drunk honesty aside,

15:37.414 --> 15:38.679
um, d-don't blame yourself.

15:38.681 --> 15:40.114
We all made mistakes.

15:40.116 --> 15:42.617
But we shouldn't let those
mistakes ruin things for Walden.

15:42.619 --> 15:44.552
Shh. You talk too much.

15:44.554 --> 15:46.354
Let's party.

15:49.392 --> 15:51.626
Lyndsey? Lyndsey?

15:53.763 --> 15:56.864
Wow, a half-naked drunk girl
is in my bed and I'm leaving.

15:56.866 --> 15:58.533
Maybe I am gay.

15:59.669 --> 16:02.236
I like to imagine the
family gathered here,

16:02.238 --> 16:04.705
eating an all-organic,
gluten-free meal

16:04.707 --> 16:07.308
of quinoa salad
and kale chips

16:07.310 --> 16:09.710
while watching the
original reality TV:

16:09.712 --> 16:12.180
a beautiful
ocean sunset.

16:12.182 --> 16:14.782
As long as this is a stable
environment for a child,

16:14.784 --> 16:16.684
I don't care
if you're eating Hot Pockets

16:16.686 --> 16:18.719
and watching&lt;i> Honey Boo Boo.&lt;/i>

16:18.721 --> 16:21.789
Uh, uh, Wally Bear, uh, can
I borrow you for a minute?

16:21.791 --> 16:24.392
Is it an emergency,
Alley Cat?

16:24.394 --> 16:28.429
Uh, it's more of a-a pickle, uh,
that needs immediate attention.

16:30.266 --> 16:31.799
Oh, it's okay. Go.

16:31.801 --> 16:34.469
Yeah, I would never come between
a man and his husband's pickle.

16:36.739 --> 16:39.273
Lyndsey's here.
She's drunk.

16:39.275 --> 16:40.408
Why?

16:40.410 --> 16:41.742
She wants to have sex with me.

16:41.744 --> 16:43.644
Why?

16:43.646 --> 16:44.879
Wait... Where is she?

16:44.881 --> 16:46.314
She's passed out in my room.

16:46.316 --> 16:48.249
Okay, okay, we-we need
to get Ms. McMartin

16:48.251 --> 16:49.851
out of here as fast as we can.

16:49.853 --> 16:51.719
Right, right. Oh, um,
by the way, when Lyndsey

16:51.721 --> 16:53.354
tried to kiss me,
I was totally into it.

16:53.356 --> 16:54.455
I don't know why I was worried.

16:54.457 --> 16:56.190
Worried about what?

16:56.192 --> 16:58.059
Nothing. Let's get her
out of here.

16:59.362 --> 17:00.728
Mm. Everything okay?

17:00.730 --> 17:03.531
Yes, we just had to reset the...
The, um...

17:03.533 --> 17:04.832
...flaven
on the stave.

17:04.834 --> 17:06.601
But, uh, everything's

17:06.603 --> 17:09.036
okay now. Uh, c-can
I get you anything?

17:09.038 --> 17:10.705
Like directions for
your drive home, or...

17:10.707 --> 17:12.507
You know, I actually
do have to get going.

17:12.509 --> 17:14.242
I did not realize it was this late.
What?

17:14.244 --> 17:15.977
No.
Oh.

17:15.979 --> 17:18.379
I'm so disappointed.
Oh.

17:18.381 --> 17:20.448
I'll just get your things
and walk you out.

17:20.450 --> 17:22.717
Oh. There we go.

17:22.719 --> 17:24.719
I got to say,
you look at that view

17:24.721 --> 17:25.920
and you never want to leave.

17:25.922 --> 17:27.855
And yet you must.

17:27.857 --> 17:29.524
Unless you want to adopt me.

17:29.526 --> 17:32.260
You're so funny.
Here's your jacket.

17:34.531 --> 17:35.696
Oh, my God.

17:35.698 --> 17:37.632
What?
Uh...

17:37.634 --> 17:39.467
This jacket,
it's-it's fantastic.

17:39.469 --> 17:42.036
What is this, wool?
I think so, yeah.

17:42.038 --> 17:44.138
Really? Because I... I would've
thought it was linen.

17:44.140 --> 17:45.873
Doesn't it feel
“linen-sy”, Alan?

17:45.875 --> 17:47.341
No, it's
definitely wool.

17:48.778 --> 17:50.645
Holy crap.
What?

17:50.647 --> 17:52.847
Uh... I forgot to
flip the cushions

17:52.849 --> 17:54.015
on the deck
furniture.

17:54.017 --> 17:55.283
Imagine the
mildew.

17:55.285 --> 17:57.485
Alan.

17:57.487 --> 17:59.687
Milady.

18:02.592 --> 18:04.659
Here we go,
almost got it.

18:04.661 --> 18:06.160
If you could
just stay still...

18:06.162 --> 18:07.595
Yeah... Oh.

18:09.799 --> 18:12.500
Uh, all right, that's it.
That wasn't so hard, was it?

18:12.502 --> 18:14.468
Actually, it was a lot harder
than it needed to be, but...

18:14.470 --> 18:16.837
That's what he said.

18:16.839 --> 18:18.906
Uh, well...
Oh, your purse.

18:18.908 --> 18:20.575
Well, thank you, guys.

18:20.577 --> 18:22.076
Uh, you'll be hearing
from me soon.

18:22.078 --> 18:23.911
Got it. Bye.

18:26.549 --> 18:27.748
Oh, my God.

18:27.750 --> 18:29.150
Is Lyndsey okay?

18:29.152 --> 18:30.885
Oh, sure. She's practically
indestructible when she's drunk.

18:30.887 --> 18:32.787
I've seen her fall down
a flight of stairs

18:32.789 --> 18:34.255
and not spill her mojito.

18:36.593 --> 18:39.860
I'm so sorry,
I forgot my phone.

18:39.862 --> 18:41.622
Oh. Here it is, right
here on the table. Hey.

18:41.637 --> 18:42.464
Oh, hey. Ho!

18:42.465 --> 18:44.098
Got it. And
get the hell out of here.

18:44.100 --> 18:47.435
Oh, one last thing. Um, I'm not
supposed to say anything,

18:47.437 --> 18:49.470
but unless something
crazy happens,

18:49.472 --> 18:50.938
you're gonna get approved.

18:51.608 --> 18:52.640
Seriously?

18:52.642 --> 18:53.908
Get out of here.

18:53.910 --> 18:55.109
Seriously.

18:55.111 --> 18:58.079
I'm here to help
with the baby.

18:58.081 --> 18:59.113
Seriously?

18:59.115 --> 19:00.314
Who is this?

19:00.316 --> 19:01.616
Uh, uh, she is...

19:01.618 --> 19:04.485
Oh, you know what,
this happens all the time.

19:04.487 --> 19:06.354
Tourists get an out-of-date
map to celebrity homes.

19:06.356 --> 19:10.825
Honey, Charlie Sheen
doesn't live here anymore.

19:10.827 --> 19:13.227
Lyndsey?

19:13.229 --> 19:14.695
Hi.

19:14.697 --> 19:15.830
And who is this?

19:15.832 --> 19:18.299
I fell down
in the sand.

19:18.301 --> 19:19.800
This is...

19:19.802 --> 19:22.136
I'm the next-door
neighbor. Hi.

19:22.138 --> 19:23.404
Uh, we were having
a get-together

19:23.406 --> 19:24.739
and this one got away.

19:24.741 --> 19:26.307
Our next-door neighbor.
That... Oh, that's right,

19:26.309 --> 19:27.375
I remember you

19:27.377 --> 19:29.243
from the Fourth of
July block party.

19:29.245 --> 19:31.779
Yeah... Oh, which, by the way,
is amazing for kids.

19:31.781 --> 19:33.314
A waterslide,
shaved ice.

19:33.316 --> 19:35.850
My waterslide's
shaved.

19:35.852 --> 19:38.386
Okay, time to go home.

19:38.388 --> 19:39.720
And, um, you know what?

19:39.722 --> 19:41.956
These guys are great.
Ask anyone on our block.

19:41.958 --> 19:43.658
We're all pulling for them
to get a kid.

19:43.660 --> 19:45.493
Thank you.
You're very sweet.

19:45.495 --> 19:46.994
Okay, here we go.

19:46.996 --> 19:48.329
No, where are you
taking me?

19:48.331 --> 19:49.463
To get a drink.

19:49.465 --> 19:51.232
Aw, you're
my best friend.

19:52.635 --> 19:55.069
Boy. Glad I never
gave her a baby.

19:55.071 --> 19:57.204
You and me both.

19:57.206 --> 19:59.273
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:04.554 --> 20:05.749
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:05.773 --> 20:07.748
Hey.
Alan,

20:07.749 --> 20:09.415
what is the one thing

20:09.417 --> 20:11.150
you've never gotten
from your mother?

20:11.152 --> 20:13.452
Uh, let's see, uh,
love, respect,

20:13.454 --> 20:15.921
a home-cooked meal,
breast milk, um...

20:15.923 --> 20:18.758
Okay, this is gonna
take too long.

20:18.760 --> 20:19.992
Approval.

20:19.994 --> 20:21.661
Wait, are-are you
trying to tell me

20:21.663 --> 20:23.262
Ms. McMartin
approved us to adopt?

20:23.264 --> 20:25.031
Yeah.
Oh, my God.

20:25.033 --> 20:26.165
Oh, my God,
that's great.

20:26.167 --> 20:28.000
I am really happy for you.

20:28.002 --> 20:30.336
Thank you. I-I couldn't
have done this without you.

20:30.338 --> 20:33.339
And so, to say thank you,
I got you a little something.

20:33.341 --> 20:35.741
Oh, you didn't have to.

20:35.743 --> 20:37.043
Oh, my God.

20:37.045 --> 20:39.645
Tickets to the &lt;i>Grease&lt;/i>
sing-along at the Bowl.

20:39.647 --> 20:40.780
You can take anyone you want.

20:40.782 --> 20:42.415
♪ You're the one that I want ♪
Aw!

20:42.417 --> 20:45.718
♪ You are the one I want,
ooh, ooh, ooh, honey ♪

20:45.720 --> 20:47.653
Fine.

20:47.655 --> 20:50.489
♪ We'll go together
like... ♪

20:50.491 --> 20:52.051
Oh, my God, I'm turning
into my husband.

20:53.600 --> 21:00.100
